name: Read real scope proposal with explicit discovery gaps and exhausted scan calls
size: 120x36
# Owned non-Git fixture. The helper checks source files and original run receipts.
require-shell: test -d @TARGET
cwd: @TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=/private/tmp/kuzushi-live-monorepo-scope-20261014/home KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/live_scope_result.py @TARGET @ART inspect
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: campaign live-scope-proposal-references-20261014
require-live-snap: 25 1 completed | completed-proposal
expect-not: L resume
nav-mode:
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 new approved plan | spent-attempt-refusal
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 Review suggested scopes | saved-proposal
expect: 2 committed / 3 total
expect: 0 context/scan
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 DRAFT SCOPES | unaccepted-boundaries
expect: Hello CLI
expect: Wave CLI
keys: Down Down f
require-live-snap: 25 Files 1..3 of 3 | loose-root-members
expect: ROOT-NOTES.md
expect: README.md
expect: Cargo.toml
ask: Does the actual model proposal retain both applications and all loose root files while keeping acceptance and scanning separate?
keys: Escape Down f
require-live-snap: 25 Files 1..2 of 2 | shared-context-members
expect: crates/greeting/src/lib.rs
keys: Escape Down f
require-live-snap: 25 Files 1..2 of 2 | uncovered-members
expect: crates/greeting/src/lib.rs
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 Uncovered | uncovered-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 Uncovered | uncovered-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 Uncovered | uncovered-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 Uncovered | uncovered-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 Uncovered | uncovered-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: uncovered-page-40x12
ask: Is it clear that shared greeting context supplies two files while those same files remain uncovered for discovery, rather than implying complete coverage?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape Up Up Up Up p
require-live-snap: 25 Accept | unaccepted-study-refusal
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/live_scope_result.py @TARGET @ART refused
ask: Does planning refuse the unaccepted revision while preserving the original failure, two spent scope requests, one protected Review call and zero scan jobs?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=/private/tmp/kuzushi-live-monorepo-scope-20261014/home KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 25 DRAFT SCOPES | recovered-boundaries
keys: Down Down Down Down f
require-live-snap: 25 Files 1..2 of 2 | recovered-coverage-gap
expect: crates/greeting/src/lib.rs
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/live_scope_result.py @TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the actual unaccepted model revision and its discovery gap without another request, acceptance or scan?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
